From a09e5f553768889056de49793744b226092580e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Leon <jan@leoncode.de>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:37:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] resolved: don't send conflict advisories on mDNS scopes

dns_scope_check_conflicts() is shared by LLMNR and mDNS. When a reply
carries a record whose key is already cached from a different sender
with different data, it queues an advisory query with the "C" bit set.
That mechanism only exists in LLMNR (RFC 4795, section 4.2).

On mDNS the "C" bit is the AA bit, which must be zero in queries
(RFC 6762, section 18.4), and several responders legitimately answer
for the same name with differing data, e.g. the SRP advertising proxies
of multiple Thread border routers publishing NSEC records with
different type bitmaps. Every responder answers the advisory, the
differing answers are taken as yet another conflict, and resolved keeps
sending queries. On a network with eleven Apple Thread border routers
this resulted in about 60 queries per second, each answered by every
border router.

Restrict the cache based conflict check to LLMNR. Conflicts with our
own records are still detected via the zone check for both protocols.

Upstream: https://github.com/systemd/systemd/commit/a09e5f553768889056de49793744b226092580e1
[Stefan: backport to v256, drop test-dns-scope unit test]
Signed-off-by: Stefan Agner <stefan@agner.ch>
---
 src/resolve/resolved-dns-scope.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/resolve/resolved-dns-scope.c b/src/resolve/resolved-dns-scope.c
index a632409..ad458d3 100644
--- a/src/resolve/resolved-dns-scope.c
+++ b/src/resolve/resolved-dns-scope.c
@@ -1268,6 +1268,7 @@ int dns_scope_notify_conflict(DnsScope *scope, DnsResourceRecord *rr) {
         int r;
 
         assert(scope);
+        assert(scope->protocol == DNS_PROTOCOL_LLMNR);
         assert(rr);
 
         /* We don't send these queries immediately. Instead, we queue
@@ -1351,6 +1352,14 @@ void dns_scope_check_conflicts(DnsScope *scope, DnsPacket *p) {
                 if (r != 0)
                         continue;
 
+                /* Advisory conflict queries only exist in LLMNR (RFC 4795, section 4.2). In mDNS several
+                 * responders may legitimately answer for the same name (e.g. the SRP advertising proxies
+                 * of Thread border routers), only conflicts with our own records matter (RFC 6762,
+                 * section 9), and queries must not have the AA bit set (RFC 6762, section 18.4). Every
+                 * responder would answer the advisory again, which we'd take as yet another conflict. */
+                if (scope->protocol != DNS_PROTOCOL_LLMNR)
+                        continue;
+
                 /* Check for conflicts against the local cache. If so,
                  * send out an advisory query, to inform everybody */
                 r = dns_cache_check_conflicts(&scope->cache, rr, p->family, &p->sender);
-- 
